<title>AUSTRIA: Asbrink repeats Sweden in good shape for EMU.</title>
<headline>Asbrink repeats Sweden in good shape for EMU.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish Finance Minister Erik Asbrink reiterated on Friday he was confident Sweden would meet European Economic and Monetary Union (EMU) entry criteria but the government would not rush into a decision on joining.</p>
<p>&quot;We have a debate going on in Sweden (about EMU) and I think the good thing is to let the debate go on for a while before we come out and make a recommendation,&quot; Asbrink said after talks with his Austrian counterpart Viktor Klima.</p>
<p>&quot;What we are trying to do is meet the convergence criteria and I am quite confident we will be able to meet them,&quot; he continued.</p>
<p>-- Vienna Newsroom, 43-1-53112-258</p>
</text>
